> It is true that this could be implemented in another way too: the client initiates pings and waits for pongs, and at the same time, the server also initiates pings and waits for pongs.

Yes, I believe this would be the expected approach by RFC. If the server is on Kestrel, the timeout APIs will be introduced as a follow-up to this one (see https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/issues/48729#issuecomment-956579982), within the same release.

